From ccc9db5958514f3d2459596f32b9eb2f3caa4d46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:37:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/38] hydra: restart the render on scene edits, and translate
 more MaterialX nodes

Implement IsStopSupported/Stop/Restart. Hosts stop the render before applying
scene edits and restart it after; without that the session kept rendering the
old scene state, so moving an object or editing a material only appeared once
the user restarted the render by hand.

Extend the MaterialX translation past standard_surface: noise and fractal,
checkerboard, position/normal/tangent lookups, mix, and the arithmetic nodes.
A mapping can now carry fixed socket values, which is how one Cycles math node
stands in for every MaterialX arithmetic node through its mode enum, and
MtlxFacOrColor picks between a texture node's scalar and colour outputs based
on what the connection feeds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
